  "findings": [
    "Complete CMAA AP 281–288 / printed 200–207 supports exactly n. 992 opening plus all fifteen proposed n. 993–996 blocks. Target signs, punctuation, capitalization and quote marks are represented under the declared calendar j/ligature/accent normalization; no new lexical prayer word lacked the complete Mame comparandum.",
    "Complete Mame AP 368–378 / printed 254–264 supplies the opening, preface dialogue, long blessing and all three oil/chrism formulas. This is a continuous complete old sequence, not an inference from scattered old ingredients. Its regular pagination and surrounding rite were read; no later insert is used.",
    "Actual Mame foecundet twice and foecundetur differ from target fecundet/fecundetur; old Pustet independently has fecund-. Mame/Pustet Unde has three crosses at per Deum, whereas target has one in bene + dico; Be + nedico/Bene + dico, added target oil/chrism signs, reduced mixture signs and punctuation/capitalization differences remain explicit. These are real target differences, not an assertion of exact historical typography or ritual identity.",
    "Mame and target print full Adesto conclusions without ejusdem. Pustet AP 287 right-column Adesto also prints its full conclusion, but with ejusdem Spiritus sancti. The short Per Dominum cue is in the neighboring Respice. The successor Latin proof corrects that specific predecessor error while preserving old source artifacts.",
